        <h3>A few staff notes</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Live Oak HefeWeizen</strong> is the beer we'd hand a visitor to prove Austin has a beer scene. Banana and clove, unfiltered, unfussy.</li>
          <li><strong>Pearl Snap</strong> and <strong>Hans' Pils</strong> are the two lagers we drink most ourselves. Crisp, clean, and they don't get old by the third one.</li>
          <li><strong>Electric Jellyfish</strong> is the hazy IPA that turned Austin onto hazy IPAs. It's the one people drive in for.</li>
          <li><strong>Shiner Bock</strong> is a Texas institution, and it's in the cave by the case because that's how it goes home.</li>
