        <h2>Seltzers and Canned Cocktails for the Lake</h2>
        <p>Boats, docks, and swim spots aren't the place for glass, and they're not the place for a shaker either. The cold cooler doors are stacked with ready-to-drink options that travel well:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Ranch Rider (Austin)</strong> &mdash; canned Ranch Water, Paloma, and Chilton made with real tequila and vodka. The Ranch Water is the closest thing to the real recipe in a can; we go deep on that in our <a href="/guides/ranch-water-guide.html">Ranch Water guide</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Lone River Ranch Water</strong> &mdash; a lighter seltzer-style take from Far West Texas, easy to drink all afternoon.</li>
          <li><strong>Topo Chico Hard Seltzer</strong> &mdash; the mineral-water brand Austin already loves, with a little kick. The tangy lemon-lime is the crowd favorite.</li>
          <li><strong>Bigger-name seltzers</strong> like White Claw, Truly, and High Noon for the group that wants variety packs.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Want to make your own Ranch Water at home? The <a href="/guides/texas-spirits-guide.html">Texas spirits guide</a> has the tequila and sotol picks.</p>

